From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:56:53 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] test(cube_hosted_legacy_vk_linux):
 DXR_CUBE_TEST_EYE_COLORS, each view cleared to its eye's colour

The same test hook as cube_handle_vk_linux, off by default: view 0 (the
left eye) is cleared red and view 1 (the right eye) blue under the
scene, so a capture of the runtime's own window tells which eye each
view reached. Used to prove the X11 declaration on a stereo window
manager, and that a swapped placement is caught.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>

Origin: vendor, https://github.com/danielcamposramos/displayxr-runtime/commit/ee0484d130eb9bac7eadc737d8c9a53895202970
Forwarded: https://github.com/danielcamposramos/displayxr-runtime/tree/order34-sbs-declare (the pull request to DisplayXR follows the answer on https://github.com/DisplayXR/displayxr-runtime/issues/1928)
Comment: Sparky Stereo OS ORDER 34; made on v2.65.0, applied to v2.66.3 without conflict.
Last-Update: 2026-11-07
---
 .../cube_hosted_legacy_vk_linux/main.cpp      | 27 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/test_apps/legacy/cube_hosted_legacy_vk_linux/main.cpp b/test_apps/legacy/cube_hosted_legacy_vk_linux/main.cpp
index 603b9b95f..f967848fe 100644
--- a/test_apps/legacy/cube_hosted_legacy_vk_linux/main.cpp
+++ b/test_apps/legacy/cube_hosted_legacy_vk_linux/main.cpp
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #include <cmath>
 #include <csignal>
 #include <cstdio>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <cstring>
 #include <string>
 #include <chrono>
@@ -1582,6 +1583,13 @@ static bool CreateSwapchainFramebuffers(VkRenderer& renderer,
     return true;
 }
 
+// TEST HOOK, off unless DXR_CUBE_TEST_EYE_COLORS=1 is set. Each view's tile is
+// cleared to its own colour before the scene is drawn: view 0 (the left eye)
+// red, view 1 (the right eye) blue. A capture of any output stage can then tell
+// which eye a view reached by its colour, e.g. the two halves a stereo
+// compositor shows of the runtime's window. Same hook as cube_handle_vk_linux.
+static bool g_testEyeColors = false;
+
 static void RenderScene(
     VkRenderer& renderer, uint32_t imageIndex,
     const EyeRenderParams* eyes, int eyeCount)
@@ -1630,6 +1638,17 @@ static void RenderScene(
         vkCmdSetViewport(cmd, 0, 1, &viewport);
         vkCmdSetScissor(cmd, 0, 1, &scissor);
 
+        if (g_testEyeColors && eye < 2) {
+            // TEST HOOK: view 0 red, view 1 blue (0 and 1 are the same in
+            // every encoding, so no sRGB conversion is needed).
+            VkClearAttachment clear = {};
+            clear.aspectMask = VK_IMAGE_ASPECT_COLOR_BIT;
+            clear.colorAttachment = 0;
+            clear.clearValue.color = {{eye == 0 ? 1.0f : 0.0f, 0.0f, eye == 0 ? 0.0f : 1.0f, 1.0f}};
+            VkClearRect rect = {scissor, 0, 1};
+            vkCmdClearAttachments(cmd, 1, &clear, 1, &rect);
+        }
+
         float vp[16];
         mat4_multiply(vp, e.projMat, e.viewMat);
 
@@ -2314,6 +2333,14 @@ int main() {
 
     LOG_INFO("=== Sim Cube OpenXR (Vulkan) ===");
 
+    if (const char* cenv = getenv("DXR_CUBE_TEST_EYE_COLORS")) {
+        g_testEyeColors = cenv[0] == '1';
+        if (g_testEyeColors) {
+            LOG_WARN("DXR_CUBE_TEST_EYE_COLORS=1 — TEST HOOK armed; view 0 (left eye) is cleared red, "
+                     "view 1 (right eye) blue");
+        }
+    }
+
     // Initialize OpenXR
     AppXrSession xr = {};
     if (!InitializeOpenXR(xr)) {
